# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  KONI — .gitignore
#  Keeps generated, fetched, and RESTRICTED data out of the public repo.
#  See README → "License & data provenance" and the NOTICE file.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# --- Python ---
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
build/
dist/
.venv/
venv/
env/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# --- OS / editor cruft ---
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp

# --- Patch backups (created by apply_flame_patch.py / apply_stream_patch.py) ---
*.bak
*.bak.*

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  KONI data — everything under data/ is built locally by the ETL or fetched
#  at runtime, and includes TLG-derived and unlicensed material that MUST NOT
#  be redistributed. Ignore the whole directory; keep the folder via .gitkeep.
#
#  This covers, among others:
#    data/raw/             cached scraped sources (incl. TLG HTML) — restricted
#    data/intermediate/    parsed per-source JSON, repo map, discovery cache
#    data/texts/           downloaded Greek TEI (CC BY-SA) — fetched at runtime
#    data/canon.json       canon built partly from restricted sources
#    data/canon.csv
#    data/diogenes.sqlite  Diogenes export of the canon (TLG-derived)
#    data/diogenes_canon.csv
#    data/bpe_vocab.json   BPE cache — rebuildable via scripts/build_bpe.py
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
data/*
!data/.gitkeep

# The LSJ build (271M of Beta Code slices + 31M of index) is fetched and built,
# not committed — but its README is: it carries the CC BY-SA 4.0 attribution
# and the build instructions, and a share-alike corpus whose provenance is not
# in the repository is a licence problem, not an omission.
!data/lexicon/
data/lexicon/*
!data/lexicon/README.md

# --- Generated analysis outputs (Flame batch / reports) ---
text_comparisons_*.html
similarity_heatmap.html
similarity_summary.tsv
linguistic_variations.tsv
dist_mat.npz

# --- Logs / temp ---
*.log
*.tmp
temp_corpus.txt

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  Claude Code — NEVER COMMIT.
#  Session state, full conversation transcripts, file history, job temp
#  files and daemon/session key material. None of it is part of the code,
#  and the transcripts can contain anything ever typed into a session.
#
#    .claude/                     local per-project settings (settings.local.json)
#    .claude-isolated-config/     full CLI state dir: jobs/, projects/ (transcripts),
#                                 file-history/, daemon/control.key, sessions/*.key,
#                                 paste-cache/, plugins/, shell-snapshots/
#    CLAUDE.md                    agent instructions, not project source
#    .claudesignore               agent-facing repo map / read bans
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.claude/
.claude-isolated-config/
CLAUDE.md
.claudesignore

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  Local-only working material — not part of the application or the README.
#
#    log.md        running development log kept by the maintainer locally
#    sideproject/  scratch sub-project (Procopius re-use): raw PDFs,
#                  pdftotext caches and Perseus TEI fetched at runtime.
#                  ~143 MB locally, and the TEI must not be redistributed
#                  (see NOTICE) — nothing in app/ or scripts/ reads it.
#    docs/         long-form notes. Not shipped; the README is the
#                  user-facing document.
#    reports/      generated by scripts/build_canon.py and
#                  scripts/build_gaps_report.py at run time — rebuildable,
#                  never a source of truth.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
log.md
sideproject/
docs/
reports/
